## Overview

ConstellAI models Earth's orbital environment as a dynamic graph, forecasts conjunctions (close-approach events) multiple days ahead, and coordinates constellation-wide avoidance maneuvers under fuel constraints — using public TLE data, orbital mechanics, temporal graph learning, and multi-agent RL.

This is a research system, not a dashboard with a model attached. Every module has an explicit physics or learning-theoretic justification, documented in [`docs/adr/`](docs/adr/).

**Target venues:** AIAA SciTech · IEEE Aerospace Conference · NeurIPS/ICLR workshops

**Core capabilities:**
- Multi-day-ahead conjunction (collision risk) forecasting via temporal graph neural networks
- Constellation-wide avoidance maneuver coordination via multi-agent reinforcement learning
- Physics-constrained optimization under fuel and mission-objective constraints
- Designed to scale toward thousands of satellites (see [Roadmap](#roadmap) for scaling strategy and known limits)

---

## Architecture

| Module | Path | Responsibility | Owner(s) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Orbital Mechanics Core (M1) | [`constellai/orbital_mechanics/`](constellai/orbital_mechanics/) | TLE ingestion, SGP4 propagation, frame transforms, perturbation models, conjunction geometry | Dev A + Dev B |
| Graph Construction (M2) | [`constellai/graph/`](constellai/graph/) | Dynamic graph construction from propagated states, temporal windowing, feature engineering | Dev C |
| TGNN Forecasting (M3) | [`constellai/models/tgnn/`](constellai/models/tgnn/) | Conjunction probability / time-to-closest-approach forecasting | Dev C |
| MARL Coordination (M4) | [`constellai/models/marl/`](constellai/models/marl/) | Coordinated avoidance maneuver policies | Dev D |
| Simulation & Evaluation (M5) | [`constellai/simulation/`](constellai/simulation/) | Independent ground-truth simulator, scenario generation, metrics | Dev A + Dev B |
| Infra / MLOps (M6) | — | Experiment tracking, CI/CD, benchmarking, reproducibility tooling | Dev D |

> **Interface contracts** between modules (units, coordinate frames, tensor shapes) are frozen in `docs/adr/` before implementation begins. Do not change an interface without an ADR update and integration-lead sign-off.

